      "writtenOn": "2025-12-01T17:16:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think we want this to be declared in just the SkCodecs namespace and be something like `MakeICCProfileUsingSKCMS` so eventually we can have `MakeICCProfileUsingRustThing` or whatever. Maybe a nested namespace like we have for text shaping stuff. `SkCodecs::skcms::MakeICCProfile` and then `SkCodecs::rust_thing::MakeICCProfile`.\n\nWhile we are bikeshedding, maybe that\u0027s something to go in a `SkColorSpaces` if that feels like a better fit.\n\nIn any case, let\u0027s set this up for a better split down the line - we\u0027ll have a header that declares the skcms-factory (factories?) and a header for the rust one and that will be a more clean separation.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 37,
        "startChar": 41,
        "endLine": 37,
        "endChar": 55
      },
      "revId": "4c631026d3f30740257f411a88fb79ce57844fab",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "78a9f04a_8de2e14d",
        "filename": "src/codec/SkCodecPriv.h",
        "patchSetId": 13
      },
      "lineNbr": 37,
      "author": {
        "id": 6035
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-12-01T21:37:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think like to keep this as-is for now (I\u0027d be fine with renaming to something, but I do think `SkCodecs::ColorProfile` is a good name for \"the color profile for a codec, that could have come from CICP, ICC, or any of the bizarro PNG things\").\n\nThe main reason is that I want the codecs themselves to all call the same `::MakeICCProfile` call, and then a flag will move the internals of that call  one implementation and the other (probably at least in some version a runtime flag, to make testing easier). One of the things that I got scared about with the `moxcms` proposal was the idea of moving individual codecs over (to be good enough to ship with one codec it needs to be good enough for all of them).",
      "parentUuid": "712e2d65_d73dffe6",
